    {
      "jobId": "296fde25-7cda-46b4-9695-657b05286ddf",
      "question": "How many stocks are in each SIC division, and what was each division's median return from January 2 to March 12, 2026?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T21:40:31.985803Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T21:41:16.094668Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**SIC Division Stock Counts and Median Returns (Jan 2 – Mar 12, 2026)**\n\n| SIC Division | Stock Count | Median Return |\n|--------------|-------------|---------------|\n| Agriculture, Forestry and Fishing | 10 | +9.39% |\n| Construction | 10 | –3.30% |\n| Finance, Insurance and Real Estate | 361 | –1.49% |\n| Manufacturing | 579 | –2.11% |\n| Mining | 64 | +17.44% |\n| Nonclassifiable | 89 | –3.40% |\n| Retail Trade | 83 | –5.07% |\n| Services | 264 | –13.41% |\n| Transportation, Communications and Utilities | 99 | +3.57% |\n| Wholesale Trade | 40 | +2.09% |\n\n[1]\n\n**Notes**\n- Returns are period returns from the first to the last available trading date within the window for each stock.\n- The \"Sector\" column in the assets table maps to the SIC division; the query groups by this field.\n- Stocks missing a price on either the window start or end date are excluded from the division's count and median calculation.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Structured retrieval result — us_equities — evidence `hermes-receipt:39cd4743afb5fb08c2b556b89fd5670041e5d650d1d9272794cfea967472448f`",
